        "AbstractText": "The specific management of the surgical risks linked to obesity, as well as technological advances combined with the standardisation of techniques, have significantly reduced the morbidity and mortality associated with bariatric surgery over recent decades. However, as with all surgery, patients are exposed to medical and surgical failures and complications."
